# tstval.ref - Expected state-consistency result for PROGRAM TSTVAL
#
# Routine under test: modern/state/stateval.f (state-consistency
#   validator over the existing nine *.COM INCLUDE headers; zero new
#   COMMON). Setup uses modern/state/stateacc.f accessors.
# DELIVERABLE - consulted/kept-in-sync in Solaris; NOT executed
#   by Blitzy.
#
# Contract: tstval.f establishes a CONSISTENT state via the SET
#   accessors, then sets a NONZERO IDIAG (the validator's first
#   executable statement is the guard IF (IDIAG .EQ. 0) RETURN, so
#   IDIAG=0 would skip every check and leave the poisoned IST
#   unchanged), then  CALL STATEVAL(IDIAG,IST)  and asserts  IST .EQ. 0
#   (consistent => status 0, zero divergences). Happy path only.
#
# Binding expectation:
EXPECT_STATUS 0
#
# Representative consistent-state SEED values (reconcile with the
# invariant in modern/state/stateval.f; reached ONLY via INCLUDE of the
# *.COM headers or via accessor CALLs - never a literal COMMON):
# /DSIO/  (mds/DSIOF.COM)
SEED_DSIO_LCW 1024
SEED_DSIO_LWORDS 2048
SEED_DSIO_NWORDS 2048
SEED_DSIO_NBUFF 8
# /DBM/   (mds/DSIOF.COM)
SEED_DBM_IDBLEN 4096
SEED_DBM_NBLOCK 64
SEED_DBM_MAXBLK 64
# /SYSTEM/ (mis/SMCOMX.COM: ISYSBF,NOUT,DUM1(37),NBPW,DUM2(14),ISPREC)
SEED_SYS_NOUT 6
SEED_SYS_NBPW 32
#
# Notes:
#  - Seeds are coherent, in-range, non-degenerate values chosen so the
#    validator's consistency relation holds (e.g. matched capacities
#    NWORDS<=LWORDS, NBLOCK<=MAXBLK); reconcile exact relation with
#    stateval.f. Avoid zeros that could read as "uninitialized".
#  - IST is poisoned to a non-zero value in the driver BEFORE the call
#    so a no-op cannot accidentally satisfy EXPECT_STATUS 0.
#  - Header-conflict caution: never mix /DSNAME/ (NASNAMES vs DSIOF) or
#    /ZZZZZZ/ (XNSTRN vs ZZZZZZ) layouts in one program unit.
#
# EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TSTVAL
